fresh-eyes: independent cold reviewer (subagent, no authorship of this branch), full scope of the four commits moving Repo onto the mdstore capability.

Verdict LAND on this tip, bee9023.

Two rounds. Round one returned DO-NOT-LAND on three items. The branch
did not compile at the revision it pinned. The escape test's move
assertion named a source file that was never created, so it failed on
ENOENT: an ambient std::fs::rename left the whole suite and all of
missouri green while a move carried an issue out of the tracker.
projects_of had no coverage, and an empty return broke nothing while a
tracker's issue count read zero in the output a person sees.

Round two verified each fix by execution. The pin builds from the
remote with no patch file. The move test no longer rests on the error
return at all: blinding both is_err assertions and keeping only the
filesystem checks still kills the ambient mutant. projects_of rejects
three mutations, including the exact pre-branch link-following
implementation this branch deleted.

Nine of twelve guards survive the suite. The reviewer applied the three
listing filters as one mutant and drove the real binary against a
project directory linked outside the tracker: the outside project is
listed and its id enumerated, and no body is reachable through show,
list or search. The filters are hardening and the handle is the
barrier, and the handle is pinned by the repaired escape test.

15 tests, clippy clean, fmt clean. The one missouri failure is a
pre-existing environment artifact, reproduced identically on the
reconstructed parent built against the old mdstore pin.

Follow-ups recorded, none blocking: load_project still answers from an
unconfined exists() and so disagrees with list_projects; one malformed
.closed aborts every project because issue_stems propagates the scan
error; the list_projects behaviour change is unpinned; and one test
calls symlink without a cfg(unix) gate.
